---@class PagleNS
local ns = select(2, ...)

-- The announcement art's atlases (ANN-R80), added to ns.ATLASES by name beside any other art's (the Curio Shop's and
-- the Modules' kits register theirs there too): where each sprite sits in its texture under media/announce/.
-- Generated by the announcements art kit's art/lib/sprites.py from the approved canvas, with the texture paths moved
-- to Pagle's; don't edit by hand. Rectangles are in texels, `scale` texels per UI unit; `box` is the drawn element inside its
-- sprite in UI units (x, y from the sprite's top left, then w, h), the rest being its shadow or glow. The kit's old
-- `crest-prestige` (Announce) and `crest-legend` (Splash) are retired, the Prestige frame and the Legend's crest drawn
-- in their place (ANN-R83, LED-R153), and so are its `toast-low` and `toast-low-ruled` pages in every toast atlas, every
-- toast being drawn full size (ANN-R80): their pixels stay in the textures unlisted.

---@class PagleAtlasSprite
---@field x integer
---@field y integer
---@field w integer
---@field h integer
---@field box number[]
---@field size number[]? its designed size in UI units, where it isn't w and h over the atlas's scale (data/CrateArt.lua)
---@field at number[]? where its top left lies from its anchor, in UI units (data/CrateArt.lua)
---@field anchor string? what `at` is from (data/CrateArt.lua)
---@field use string? what the sprite is for: "tint", "add", "fixed", "cap", "mirror", "slice" (data/CrateArt.lua)
---@field alpha number? the opacity to draw a sprite stored at full alpha at (data/CrateArt.lua)
---@field tint number[]? the colour, 0 to 255, it is drawn in when not a tier's (data/CrateArt.lua)

---@class PagleAtlas
---@field file string
---@field width integer
---@field height integer
---@field scale number
---@field sprites table<string, PagleAtlasSprite>

